# %(title)s — the manifest of a .finn package.
#
# A package says what it is called, what it installs and what runs it.
# The shape is the one the application registry uses, because it answers
# the same question: the name the user sees, the icon, and the command.
#
#   id       the name the rest of the system uses
#   name     what the user sees
#   icon     an SVG in /usr/share/finn/icons
#   command  what to run when the app is launched
#   version  the version of the package
#   summary  free text, shown as the app's detail line
#
# The .finn format itself is not implemented yet — finnpkg is a stub — so
# this is the manifest the SDK writes, and the package format is a design
# that has not been settled.

id      | %(id)s
name    | %(title)s
icon    | %(id)s.svg
command | /usr/bin/finn-%(id)s
version | 0.1.0
summary | %(title)s
